  "title": "c-VEP dataset from Thielen et al. (2021)",
  "description": "This dataset contains 8-channel EEG recordings from 30 healthy participants performing a code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) brain-computer interface task. Participants fixated on target cells in a 20-symbol calculator grid while all cells flashed with pseudo-random Gold code sequences. The data support work on reducing BCI calibration, from full training to zero training, using an encoding model based on reconvolution.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 512 Hz from 8 sintered Ag/AgCl active electrodes (Biosemi ActiveTwo). Each of 30 participants completed 5 blocks of 20 trials of 31.5 s each. Stimuli were luminance-modulated Gold codes (126 bits) shown on an iPad Pro at 60 Hz. Classification used template matching with a reconvolution encoding model.",
